    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a4836cca1208c95",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "45fe9141623d6a0d068851c1e8773c43f14232e25e1499ff2bad441631271d69",
      "text": "Arrival in Manaus. You will be met by our English-speaking guide and transferred to the pier  in a comfortable, air-conditioned vehicle. Then you will have a unique adventure - a seaplane flight (about 30 min) from the pier to Mirante do Gavião Lodge. You will enjoy your trip admiring breathtaking views of the Amazon  rivers and jungles above. Your luggage will be transported (about 3 hr) to the lodge by car.\n\nThen you can have wildlife viewing excursions (on foot or by boat). These activities are led by naturalist guides. \n\nOptional: a diving activity  in the Rio Negro. \n\nDinner at Camu Camu Restaurant. The Camu Camu Restaurant overlooks the river, and offers a mix of regional flavors. These include locally-sources fresh fruits and nuts, prawns, and fish.\n\nAfter dinner, you can spot caimans and other nocturnal animals, and explore interpretative trails in the Anavilhanas National Park, a Brazilian protected area in the state of Amazonas. The region is one of the most unique and well-preserved ecosystems in the world, with astounding biodiversity.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1R7vGukYEs1KtuFdB3ugkR_BDSej2GtjT",
        "documentSha256": "87652d54eed7f53278892226559d7d615d8b3f0390ad417a8985975c8059f494",
